{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_critical-security-vulnerability-in-react-server-com","statement":"Lachlan Davidson reported a security vulnerability in React on November 29th that allows unauthenticated remote code execution by exploiting a flaw in how React decodes payloads sent to React Server Function endpoints.","source_span":"On November 29th, Lachlan Davidson reported a security vulnerability in React that allows unauthenticated remote code execution by exploiting a flaw in how React decodes payloads sent to React Server Function endpoints."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_critical-security-vulnerability-in-react-server-com","statement":"The vulnerability was disclosed as CVE-2025-55182 and is rated CVSS 10.0.","source_span":"This vulnerability was disclosed as CVE-2025-55182 ... and is rated CVSS 10.0."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_critical-security-vulnerability-in-react-server-com","statement":"The vulnerability is present in versions 19.0, 19.1.0, 19.1.1, and 19.2.0 of react-server-dom-webpack, react-server-dom-parcel, and react-server-dom-turbopack.","source_span":"The vulnerability is present in versions 19.0, 19.1.0, 19.1.1, and 19.2.0 of:"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_critical-security-vulnerability-in-react-server-com","statement":"A fix for the critical RCE vulnerability was introduced in versions 19.0.1, 19.1.2, and 19.2.1.","source_span":"A fix was introduced in versions 19.0.1, 19.1.2, and 19.2.1."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_critical-security-vulnerability-in-react-server-com","statement":"The affected React frameworks and bundlers include Next.js, React Router, Waku, @parcel/rsc, @vitejs/plugin-rsc, and rwsdk.","source_span":"The following React frameworks & bundlers are affected: next, react-router, waku, @parcel/rsc, @vitejs/plugin-rsc, and rwsdk."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_critical-security-vulnerability-in-react-server-com","statement":"If an app's React code does not use a server, or the app does not use a framework, bundler, or bundler plugin that supports React Server Components, the app is not affected by the vulnerability.","source_span":"If your app’s React code does not use a server, your app is not affected by this vulnerability."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_critical-security-vulnerability-in-react-server-com","statement":"Next.js users on version 13.3 or later of Next.js 13 should upgrade to version 14.2.35.","source_span":"If you are on version `13.3` or later version of Next.js 13 (`13.3.x`, `13.4.x`, or `13.5.x`) please upgrade to version `14.2.35`."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_critical-security-vulnerability-in-react-server-com","statement":"The update instructions note, updated January 26, 2026, lists additional vulnerabilities: CVE-2025-55184 and CVE-2025-67779 (DoS, High, CVSS 7.5), CVE-2025-55183 (Source Code Exposure, Medium, CVSS 5.3), and CVE-2026-23864 (DoS, dated January 26, 2026, CVSS 7.5).","source_span":"Denial of Service - High Severity: CVE-2025-55184 and CVE-2025-67779 (CVSS 7.5) ... Source Code Exposure - Medium Severity: CVE-2025-55183 (CVSS 5.3) ... Denial of Service - High Severity: January 26, 2026 CVE-2026-23864 (CVSS 7.5)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_critical-security-vulnerability-in-react-server-com","statement":"This blog post was published December 3, 2025 by The React Team.","source_span":"December 3, 2025 by [The React Team](/community/team)"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_critical-security-vulnerability-in-react-server-com","fact_refs":[0],"question":"Who reported the critical React Server Components RCE vulnerability, and when was it reported?","answer":"Lachlan Davidson reported it on November 29th, exploiting a flaw in how React decodes payloads sent to React Server Function endpoints."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_critical-security-vulnerability-in-react-server-com","fact_refs":[1],"question":"What CVE ID and CVSS score were assigned to the critical React Server Components vulnerability?","answer":"It was disclosed as CVE-2025-55182 and rated CVSS 10.0."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_critical-security-vulnerability-in-react-server-com","fact_refs":[2,3],"question":"Which versions of react-server-dom-webpack, react-server-dom-parcel, and react-server-dom-turbopack were affected by CVE-2025-55182, and which versions contain the fix?","answer":"Versions 19.0, 19.1.0, 19.1.1, and 19.2.0 were vulnerable; fixes were released in versions 19.0.1, 19.1.2, and 19.2.1."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_critical-security-vulnerability-in-react-server-com","fact_refs":[4],"question":"Which frameworks and bundlers were affected by the critical React Server Components vulnerability?","answer":"Next.js, React Router, Waku, @parcel/rsc, @vitejs/plugin-rsc, and rwsdk were affected."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_critical-security-vulnerability-in-react-server-com","fact_refs":[5],"question":"Under what condition is an app not affected by the React Server Components RCE vulnerability?","answer":"If the app's React code does not use a server, or it does not use a framework, bundler, or bundler plugin that supports React Server Components, it is not affected."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_critical-security-vulnerability-in-react-server-com","fact_refs":[6],"question":"To which Next.js version should users running Next.js 13.3 or later upgrade to fix the RCE vulnerability?","answer":"They should upgrade to version 14.2.35."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_critical-security-vulnerability-in-react-server-com","fact_refs":[7],"question":"What additional CVEs were added to the critical vulnerability's update instructions as of the January 26, 2026 update?","answer":"CVE-2025-55184 and CVE-2025-67779 (Denial of Service, High, CVSS 7.5), CVE-2025-55183 (Source Code Exposure, Medium, CVSS 5.3), and CVE-2026-23864 (Denial of Service, dated January 26, 2026, CVSS 7.5)."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_denial-of-service-and-source-code-exposure-in-react","statement":"This post was published December 11, 2025 by The React Team, and updated January 26, 2026.","source_span":"December 11, 2025 by The React Team ... _Updated January 26, 2026._"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_denial-of-service-and-source-code-exposure-in-react","statement":"Security researchers found and disclosed two additional vulnerabilities in React Server Components while attempting to exploit the patches for the prior critical vulnerability.","source_span":"Security researchers have found and disclosed two additional vulnerabilities in React Server Components while attempting to exploit the patches in last week’s critical vulnerability."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_denial-of-service-and-source-code-exposure-in-react","statement":"The new vulnerabilities do not allow Remote Code Execution, and the patch for the original critical vulnerability remains effective at mitigating the RCE exploit.","source_span":"These new vulnerabilities do not allow for Remote Code Execution. The patch for React2Shell remains effective at mitigating the Remote Code Execution exploit."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_denial-of-service-and-source-code-exposure-in-react","statement":"The Denial of Service vulnerabilities were disclosed as CVE-2025-55184, CVE-2025-67779, and CVE-2026-23864, all High Severity with CVSS 7.5.","source_span":"Denial of Service - High Severity: CVE-2025-55184, CVE-2025-67779, and CVE-2026-23864 (CVSS 7.5)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_denial-of-service-and-source-code-exposure-in-react","statement":"The Source Code Exposure vulnerability was disclosed as CVE-2025-55183, Medium Severity, CVSS 5.3.","source_span":"Source Code Exposure - Medium Severity: CVE-2025-55183 (CVSS 5.3)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_denial-of-service-and-source-code-exposure-in-react","statement":"Patches published as versions 19.0.3, 19.1.4, and 19.2.3 were incomplete and required a further update.","source_span":"If you updated to 19.0.3, 19.1.4, and 19.2.3, these are incomplete, and you will need to update again."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_denial-of-service-and-source-code-exposure-in-react","statement":"Fixes were backported to versions 19.0.4, 19.1.5, and 19.2.4.","source_span":"Fixes were backported to versions 19.0.4, 19.1.5, and 19.2.4."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_denial-of-service-and-source-code-exposure-in-react","statement":"For React Native users in a monorepo, only react-server-dom-webpack, react-server-dom-parcel, and react-server-dom-turbopack need to be updated, not react or react-dom.","source_span":"If you are using React Native in a monorepo, you should update _only_ the impacted packages if they are installed ... you do not need to update `react` and `react-dom`"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_denial-of-service-and-source-code-exposure-in-react","statement":"CVE-2026-23864, dated January 26, 2026 with base score 7.5 (High), covers additional DoS vulnerabilities discovered still present in React Server Components; patches published January 26th mitigate them.","source_span":"CVEs: CVE-2026-23864 ... Base Score: 7.5 (High) ... Date: January 26, 2026 ... The patches published January 26th mitigate these DoS vulnerabilities."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_denial-of-service-and-source-code-exposure-in-react","statement":"The original fix for CVE-2025-55184 was incomplete, leaving earlier versions vulnerable; versions 19.0.4, 19.1.5, and 19.2.4 are safe.","source_span":"The original fix addressing the DoS in CVE-2025-55184 was incomplete. This left previous versions vulnerable. Versions 19.0.4, 19.1.5, 19.2.4 are safe."}
